+
+Base frontend gate: `base-sso-history-units.log`, 18 script tests, semantic
+contrast check and 94 Vitest tests (21 files), plus lint/typecheck and README/hub
+validators. Rust/backend release gates were not rerun for this frontend checkpoint.
+
+Current browser run uses built source with mocked HTTP/OIDC, not deployed images:
+
+- 120 page captures across four routes, three themes and ten widths; shell,
+  reading/detail geometry and main control targets remain checked.
+- 30 project edit modal captures across gray/dark/light and
+  375/767/768/1023/1024/1279/1280/1440/1920/2560 px. Dialog fits the viewport,
+  draft survives resizing, visible targets meet 40/44 px and discard returns focus.
+- Five additional controlled captures: issue save failure, project create failure,
+  partial catalog refresh with retained readonly draft, cached access revocation
+  and cold not-found. Total: 155 PNG files.
+- Cached 503 retains rows/draft but blocks writes; cancellation remains usable.
+  Cached 403 hides rows/CRUD, and cold 404 has neither CRUD nor retry.
+- Search retains extra query/hash, resets page, survives direct SSO/reload/Back.
+  Dirty close cancellation returns focus to the field. Async POST allows one
+  submission, blocks Escape/close, retains failure values; confirmed success
+  closes the form and reaches board without a false dirty-navigation prompt.
+- Unit fixtures additionally verify dirty navigation/beforeunload, same-ID refetch,
+  new-session initialization and cancellation of unavailable delete confirmation.
+
+Final modal mobile and partial/denied desktop captures were inspected visually.
+Artifacts: [current captures](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-projects-verified-browser/),
+[current browser log](../../../../audit-artifacts/base-standard-2026-10-01/task-projects-verified-browser.log).
+Earlier `task-projects-browser` and `task-projects-final-browser` runs contain
+superseded failures; they are not green acceptance evidence. Local worker/color
+warnings remain in logs; unit parallelism was bounded after a host-load timeout.
+
+Generic project API error messages still expose English technical text. Full
+route/role/state/console/network matrix, actual images, live SSO, backend gates,
+real README provenance, consumer snapshot synchronization, default integration
+and mirror remain required. All original findings remain open until release proof.
+Playwright-owned preview stopped after terminal completion; port 18865 had no listener.
+No GitHub/fetch/push, protected runtime changes or foreign checkout edits.
